            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "David has 13 marbles. Five of them are pink, three are blue, three are green and two are black. If he chooses a marble at random, what is the probability that it is green?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{3}{13}$",
      "worked": "There are 3 green marbles among 13 marbles, and each marble is equally likely to be chosen.\n\n$$P(\\text{green})=\\frac{\\text{number of green marbles}}{\\text{total number of marbles}}=\\frac{3}{13}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
